      },
      "message": "feat(tools)!: cutting data by work material - Unknown default row, stepdown/stepover, stock material\n\nEvery tool's cutting data now has an Unknown row (material None, file\nword \"unknown\"): what the tool runs when no row names the material in\nforce, and the fallback for a row's missing stepdown/stepover. It is\nderived from the tool's own rpm/feed and stored only when it says\nsomething more, so plain tools, v62 projects and v1/v2 .camtools files\nload and save unchanged, their own rpm/feed read as the Unknown row.\n\nRows may state a stepdown and a stepover (mm). They seed an operation\nonly inside an undoable command (quick-add, MCP add_operation, the\nrecognizer, SetWorkMaterial, SetStockMaterial, a tool retarget), never on\nload; a stepover wider than the cutter is refused by tool name.\n\nA setup's stock may state its workpiece material (StockMaterial,\nSetStockMaterial, MCP set_stock_material, stock page Material group).\nThe row is picked by the stock's material, then the document's, then\nUnknown. The tool's running rpm/feed (the posted S word) follow the\ndocument material only.\n\nThe tool page's cutting data is a table of material, rpm, feed,\nstepdown and stepover, with the Unknown row first.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: projects are written as version 63, and tool libraries\nholding a stated Unknown row or a step as version 3; older builds refuse\nthem.\n\nFixes #2015\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
